"_score_margin_advantage":27.4,"_gate_pool_share":-0.3131049652507243,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.06884330516963422,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":59.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.026337239229272225,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":38.2,"_gate_margins":0.0028656386110918614,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":52.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06215014711091617,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":80.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.002350490105011982,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":52.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.003745531979618222,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.3309,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Enterprise Products Partners L.P. provides midstream energy services to producers and consumers of natural gas, natural gas liquids (NGLs), crude oil, petrochemicals, and refined products. It operates in four segments: NGL Pipelines & Services; Crude Oil Pipelines & Services; Natural Gas Pipelines & Services; and Petrochemical & Refined Products Services. The NGL Pipelines & Services segment offers natural gas processing and related NGL marketing activities. This segment operates natural gas processing facilities located in Colorado, Louisiana, Mississippi, New Mexico, Texas, and Wyoming; NGL pipelines; NGL fractionation facilities; NGL and related product storage facilities; and NGL marine terminals. The Crude Oil Pipelines & Services segment operates crude oil pipelines; and crude oil storage and marine terminals, which include a fleet of approximately 200 tractor-trailer tank trucks that are used to transport crude oil. It also engages in crude oil marketing activities. The Natural Gas Pipelines & Services segment operates natural gas pipeline systems to gather, treat, and transport natural gas. It leases underground salt dome natural gas storage facilities in Napoleonville, Louisiana; owns an underground salt dome storage cavern in Wharton County, Texas; and transports, stores, and markets natural gas. The Petrochemical & Refined Products Services segment operates propylene fractionation facilities, including propylene fractionation units and propane dehydrogenation facilities, and related marketing activities; butane isomerization complex and related deisobutanizer operations; and octane enhancement, isobutane dehydrogenation, and high purity isobutylene production facilities. It also operates refined products pipelines and terminals; and ethylene export terminals; and provides refined products marketing and marine transportation services. The company was founded in 1968 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. A. James Teague | Co-CEO & Director of Enterprise Products Holdings LLC | Age 80 | Compensation: $6.9M (FY2025)","financial_summary":["Enterprise Products Partners L. is a large-cap energy business with a $82.6B market cap on $52.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","The business throws off $3.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.48\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 33% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 49% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4943106889099696},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","27 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"A December Rate Hike Looks Likely: Buy These 3 Energy and Materials Dividend Stocks Before the Fed Moves","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/december-rate-hike-looks-likely-173050000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794591320.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.372,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"6 Energy Dividend Stocks Yielding Up to 7.97% That Income Investors Should Know","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/6-energy-dividend-stocks-yielding-160824000.html"